/// UUIDs matching Python's `uuid` module, implemented in pure Koala.
///
/// Generation: `uuid4()` (random), `uuid7()` (time-ordered, RFC 9562),
/// `uuid5(ns, name)` (SHA-1) and `uuid3(ns, name)` (MD5).
///
/// Parsing and formatting live on the `UUID` value type, whose member names
/// follow Python's: `hex()`, `to_bytes()`, `urn()`, `version()`, `variant()`,
/// `fields()`, `time_low()`, `time_mid()`, `time_hi_version()`,
/// `clock_seq_hi_variant()`, `clock_seq_low()`, `node()`, `time()`,
/// `clock_seq()` and `bytes_le()`.
///
/// Two Python details cannot be carried over, and the difference is
/// deliberate:
///   - Koala has no computed properties, so every Python attribute is a
///     method here: `u.hex` becomes `u.hex()`;
///   - `int` is 64-bit, so a UUID's 128-bit `int` form is not offered; use
///     `hex()`, `to_str()` or `to_bytes()` instead.
///
/// `print(u)` and `format("{}", u)` yield the canonical 36-character text,
/// the same as Python's `str(u)`.
///
/// Example:
///     let u = uuid.uuid4()
///     print(u)                            // 0f8fad5b-d9cb-469f-a165-70867728950e
///     print(u.version(), u.variant())     // 4 specified in RFC 4122
///     let v = uuid.UUID("0f8fad5bd9cb469fa16570867728950e")
///     print(v == u)                       // true
///     print(uuid.uuid5(uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS, "www.widgets.com"))
///     // 3d813cbb-47fb-50d8-9ed5-1ab7bd8f7dbe